{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence","id":460187,"title":"Four dots of Influence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-28T11:00:20-07:00","id":460187,"title":"Four dots of Influence","content":"So the mechanics for Influence powers are starting to make sense to me. In thinking over them today, though, I started wondering about the Create and Mass Create powers, though.<br /> For the first few dots worth of powers, having time limits on them makes a lot of sense. When you use your Influence to Create something phsysical, though, like water or earth or something, does it just blink out of existence again when the few minutes you get from successes are up? That's how it works in Ars Magica, but it's not explicitly spelled out here other than to say that you can create a thing permanantly with Mass Create.<br /> <br /> Anyone already thought this through or know the answers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T11:09:33-07:00","id":460216,"title":"","content":"Per the extrapolations of artificial spirit Influence in Lore of the Forsaken p137-8, bearing in mind possible obsolescence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Create (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The spirit can create a new example of its sphere of influence. The cost is four Essence. The new creation lasts for one hour per success, before <b>fading back into ephemera</b>. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T11:50:35-07:00","id":460241,"title":"","content":"Well that's helpful. How long does it say Strengthening, Manipulations, and Control all last?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T11:58:44-07:00","id":460257,"title":"","content":"One minute per success, ten minutes per success, and ten minutes per success. Mass Create gives a time of one day per success, which means these durations loosely correspond to the durations for extra dots of Influence.<br /> <br /> I wasn't kidding when I mentioned possible obsolescence; <i>Lore</i> was the fourth book of 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T16:02:48-07:00","id":460457,"title":"","content":"It fades out of existence. You need Influence 5 to create permanently, and it's actually listed that way under Mass Create in the 2nd edition core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T13:43:59-07:00","id":461414,"title":"","content":"I saw the note under Mass Create. It seemed like a really weird shift to the system:<br /> To Strengthen something permanently you need 5 dots.<br /> To have a Maniplulation last permanently you need 6 dots.<br /> To have a Control you set in place last permanently you need 7 dots.<br /> To have something you Create become permanent you need 5 dots.<br /> <br /> Things Created with 4 dots last mere minutes. Things Created with 5 dots last forever.<br /> Things Mass Created with 5 dots last mere minutes, with no suggestion that anything less than 9 dots could make them permanent.<br /> <br /> I mean, I know its spirit powers and its supposed to be weird, but it seems so unfleshed out for a set of powers with multiple lines of access (Gift of the Elementals, Wellspring Rite, Shadow Maquerade from the Crescent Moon Gift...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:16:59-07:00","id":461452,"title":"","content":"\u2026Influences above five dots do not work that way. The Celestines can mess with <i>templates</i> and greater Incarnae are, in Mage's terms, Masters of the [Their Influence] Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:49:34-07:00","id":461508,"title":"","content":"You can mass create permanently with 5 dots. It just takes a lot of essence and a lot of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:04:50-07:00","id":461546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence?p=461508#post461508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can mass create permanently with 5 dots. It just takes a lot of essence and a lot of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>By which you mean premantently create each unit of the Mass one at a time for 5 essence each? That hardly seems in keeping with the theme of Mass Create...<br /> <br /> As to my chart earlier, it's based on adding the extra duration dots in from page 186. To get to Permanent, you need to add four dots, which means after the one dot power (Strengthen), you'd theoretically need more than five dots to get there. And since anything with 6+ dots is basically a god-being, it seems weird to have a system that so quickly demands that.<br /> <br /> As to how 6+ dots actually, works, I've read Imperial Mysteries, so I know what 6+ dots of the Arcana mean. But this isn't Mage and these aren't Mage powers. Are they supposed to be the same?<br /> Is Lore of the Forsaken the most in depth discussion of how they're planning to have these work at the moment? If so, is there going to be an update?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:39:07-07:00","id":461603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence?p=461546#post461546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to my chart earlier, it's based on adding the extra duration dots in from page 186. To get to Permanent, you need to add four dots, which means after the one dot power (Strengthen), you'd theoretically need more than five dots to get there. And since anything with 6+ dots is basically a god-being, it seems weird to have a system that so quickly demands that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulate and Control are not things that really <i>need</i> durational expansion to permanent for their most direct applications, particularly not for beings with improvisational capacity at their disposal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to how 6+ dots actually, works, I've read Imperial Mysteries, so I know what 6+ dots of the Arcana mean. </div> </div> </div>Do you know what &quot;regains their Rank in Essence per <i>turn</i>&quot; means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:11:29-07:00","id":461621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence?p=461603#post461603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you know what &amp;quot;regains their Rank in Essence per <i>turn</i>&amp;quot; means?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems straightforward enough, but it's not written in Werewolf 2E anywhere. Or Imperial Mysteries, for that matter, since you left in my quote referencing that.<br /> My main question here is &quot;where is this fleshed out?&quot; You clearly know more about this than me. Is this coming from Lore of the Forsaken? Book of Spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:30:06-07:00","id":461630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460187-four-dots-of-influence?p=461621#post461621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems straightforward enough, but it's not written in Werewolf 2E anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That thing where one of the causes of a Barren is <i>the presence of a godlike spirit</i> would seem to indicate that the Essence is going <i>somewhere obvious</i> given the reference to lesser spirits tithing their Essence up the Ranks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or Imperial Mysteries, for that matter, since you left in my quote referencing that. </div> </div> </div>Page 55. &quot;Godlike spirits have ever-renewing supplies of Essence, having a maximum of 25 x Rank and regaining their Rank per turn.&quot; Kind of puts a damper on claims that brute-forcing permanent Mass Create is out of keeping with its more temporary main use; they're not called ephemeral beings for the innate enduring solidity of their powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main question here is &quot;where is this fleshed out?&quot; You clearly know more about this than me. Is this coming from Lore of the Forsaken? Book of Spirits? </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries is the only book at present that covers the capabilities of godlike spirits beyond the point of &quot;they're plot devices&quot; and was co-written by the guy who devised the 2e Ephemeral Beings rules. The capabilities outlined therein are within spec for what the tribal totems and similarly potent spirits have been described as capable of in various places throughout Werewolf, including, yes, Lore. There's also this bit in War Against the Pure's &quot;generational game,&quot; which is about as explicit as one can get:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p75</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a mage, you may not know much about the Awakened and their Supernal magic, but you don\u2019t particularly have to. If you do not have Mage: The Awaken[ing] and don\u2019t care to pick it up, just make up a few neat spells that don\u2019t have the same natural, animistic feel as werewolf Gifts. In fact, spells are quite like spirits\u2019 Influence ratings, with an extra focus on acquiring knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're looking for a specific blow-by-blow outline of what godlike Influence can do in Werewolf that isn't &quot;use the Practices of Awakened magic as a guideline and convert costs to Essence&quot; then you're out of luck for the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-29-2015, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:32:26-07:00","id":462117,"title":"","content":"I think you could probably argue that the single permanent creation a spirit is capable of at essence 5 marks the beginning of the exponential growth in potency they experience past that point.<br /> <br /> We're talking about an entity on the cusp of godhood. That's where you'd expect the rules to start breaking down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":".  typo 03-30-2015, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:11:18-07:00","id":462846,"title":"","content":"It's a weird shift but I think it makes sense; creating something permanently that's a typical example of that phenomenon is something fairly typical for the world, most likely, whereas permanently controlling something can mean things like fire floating through the air unnaturally, completely breaking normal laws of physics. Creating fire 'permanently' wouldn't do that, it'd just be a normal fire that'd need to be extinguished normally instead of eventually dissipating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}